From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:35:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] riskmandate-android-demo.build@PrompTugal.angelo: X-Ray
 WebView rastered ahead, renderer at important priority

Angelo, 11 Nov about 23:05 UTC, on 0.1.165: "There's also a quite evident lag in processing the
graphical elements of the dashboard, not sure if that can't be helped or there is a fix?"

Our part of the rendering path: offscreen pre-raster on, renderer priority important (not waived
when briefly not visible). Hardware acceleration was already on (no opt-out in the manifest), and no
Compose layer with alpha sits over the WebView (only the 28x64 dp exit tab fades). The rest of the
lag is the page's own weight (about 10,000 DOM nodes on X-Ray, six backdrop blurs): build3/build.md.
His other findings (the menu, the white band, the language) are in the page, not the app; Swarm
empty was 0.1.165's host list, fixed in 5badada.

Not run in this session (Gradle on the clone was refused by the session's permission check):
./gradlew testDebugUnitTest lintDebug assembleRelease bundleRelease. The check step runs it.

